# clang-tidy configuration for emil.
#
# Checks are opt-out from clang-tidy's defaults.  One exclusion, and a
# reason for it:
#
#   security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#     Demands the C11 Annex K functions -- memcpy_s, snprintf_s,
#     memset_s.  emil targets C99 (SS1.2), Annex K is optional even in
#     C11, and glibc does not implement it, so the check cannot be
#     satisfied on any platform emil supports.  It fired 159 times
#     against 30 files while the only two real findings in the tree
#     sat in the same output, which is the actual cost: an analysis
#     stage nobody can read is an analysis stage nobody runs.
#
# Bounds safety for the calls this check flags is carried by the dbuf
# and abuf allocators (SS6) and by the review rules in tests/, not by
# a libc extension that does not exist here.
Checks: '-clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling'
